{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3303","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3303","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3303\",\"parent_revision\":\"51717bd3781798091acc922414b19b6d1c2f9e91f9b846ed525f843143ec8d92\",\"root_revision\":\"51717bd3781798091acc922414b19b6d1c2f9e91f9b846ed525f843143ec8d92\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nTwo small, pre-existing, unrelated code-quality gaps surfaced while working on #3277 but explicitly kept out of that fix's scope:\\n\\n1. `dh_core/operations.py::create_plan` is annotated `-> CreatePlanResult` and its body only ever returns `CreatePlanResult`, yet `sam_schema/server.py` and `sam_schema/sam_plan.py` both do `isinstance(result, CreatePlanError)` on that return value. `CreatePlanError`'s own docstring claims it's returned \\\"on the ArtifactWriteError path\\\" but that path doesn't appear to exist in the current body (ArtifactWriteError now appears to be raised, not caught-and-converted). These look like dead isinstance checks left over from a prior implementation \u2014 someone should confirm whether they're truly dead and remove them, or find the missing path that should produce them.\\n\\n2. `sam_plan.py`'s `append-task` CLI command doesn't catch `TaskValidationError` even though it's genuinely raised by every backend's `append_task` for duplicate task IDs (confirmed in local_yaml.py, github_task.py, beads.py, _utils.py) \u2014 a duplicate-ID append via CLI today produces a raw traceback instead of a clean error exit. Reasonable one-line fix: add `TaskValidationError` to that command's except-tuple.\\n\\nUser-provided context: no fix attempted yet \u2014 these are flagged findings from three independent reviewers (architect, code-reviewer, quality-reviewer) during #3277's implementation, not yet investigated for a root cause.\\n\\n## Context\\n\